From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] oggdec: a header packet kept up to 256 KB, not whole

An Ogg stream's comment header can carry a cover as text
(METADATA_BLOCK_PICTURE, base64): megabytes in one packet. The demuxer
gathered the whole packet in the stream's buffer, which doubles as it grows
(the old and the new one held together for a moment), and the picture was
then decoded into yet another buffer: about three times its size. An Opus
file with a 4 MB cover couldn't be opened on a player with 10 MB to spare,
for its tags or to play it.

While a stream is still reading its headers, once OGG_HEADER_KEEP bytes of
a packet are buffered, a page that is only the middle of that packet (every
segment 255: it neither starts nor ends in the page) is dropped after its
checksum is verified. The packet's last page is read as ever, so the packet
ends where it should, cut short in the middle. The comment parser already
stops at a comment longer than what is left ("truncated comment header"):
the comments before the cut are read, the cut one is left out.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [a small player's limits]

--- a/libavformat/oggdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/oggdec.c
@@ -295,6 +295,8 @@
             return 1;
     return 0;
 }
+
+#define OGG_HEADER_KEEP (256 * 1024)   /* Fathom: see ogg_read_page() */
 
 static int buf_realloc(struct ogg_stream *os, int size)
 {
@@ -427,6 +429,25 @@
         return 0;
     }
 
+    /* Fathom: a header packet is kept up to OGG_HEADER_KEEP and no more.
+     * A comment header can carry a cover as text, megabytes of it, and the
+     * whole packet was gathered in a buffer that doubled as it grew: more
+     * memory than a small player has, and the end of the file when there
+     * wasn't enough. Past that size, a page that is nothing but the middle
+     * of such a packet (it neither starts nor ends in it) is let go as if
+     * it had never been read. The packet's last page still comes, so it
+     * ends where it should, short: its comments up to the one cut are read
+     * as ever, and that one is left out as truncated. */
+    if (idx >= 0 && os->header && os->incomplete && (flags & OGG_FLAG_CONT) &&
+        nsegs > 0 && os->bufpos - os->pstart >= OGG_HEADER_KEEP) {
+        for (i = 0; i < nsegs && segments[i] == 255; i++)
+            ;
+        if (i == nsegs) {
+            *sid = -1;
+            return 0;
+        }
+    }
+
     /* CRC is correct so we can be 99% sure there's an actual change here */
     if (idx < 0) {
         if (data_packets_seen(ogg))
